---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { event } from '../data/catalogue';
import '../styles/event-actions.css';
---

<Layout title="Your email and event reminders" noIndex>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="reminder-page">
      <p class="event-kicker">Just this event</p>
      <h1>
        Your email.
        <br />
        Your choice.
      </h1>
      <div class="reading-copy">
        <p>
          The {event.series} organiser uses the email address you provide to
          confirm your request, send the remaining event reminders and
          communicate essential changes about this event.
        </p>
        <h2>What we keep</h2>
        <p>
          Your email address, confirmation and permission dates, the wording you
          agreed to, unsubscribe status and delivery records. We use short-lived
          request limits to help prevent abuse. You do not need an account, and
          your address and signup totals are not shown on the public website.
        </p>
        <h2>How it is used</h2>
        <p>
          Reminder information is kept separately from participant profiles.
          Only authorised organisers and the services that store or deliver the
          reminders can process it. We do not add you to a future mailing list
          or use tracking pixels in these emails.
        </p>
        <h2>Stop reminders</h2>
        <p>
          Use the unsubscribe link in any reminder, without signing in. We will
          stop future reminders. You can also contact the organiser to ask about
          your information.
        </p>
        <h2>Retention and delivery services</h2>
        <p>
          Pending requests expire after seven days. Campaign addresses are
          scheduled for removal 30 days after the event. Limited consent,
          suppression records remain for up to 60 days. Service backups may
          retain copies under each provider’s retention rules.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cloudflare hosts the signup form, Supabase stores the private reminder
          records, and Google Gmail sends the emails from Timothi Lim on behalf
          of the organising team. Email copies and replies in Gmail remain until
          the organiser deletes them; the 30-day database cleanup does not
          delete mailbox copies. Contact the organiser if you would like those
          removed.
        </p>
        {event.publicContact && (
          <p>
            Contact:{' '}
            <a href={`mailto:${event.publicContact.email}`}>
              {event.publicContact.email}
            </a>
            .
          </p>
        )}
        <a class="text-link" href="/reminders/">
          Back to event reminders
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>
  .reading-copy {
    max-width: 65ch;
  }
  .reading-copy h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
</style>
